<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75881" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ μὲν οὖν</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐμενοῦν</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>on the contrary . . not</i> . . , introducing a neg.
			statement in contradiction or correction of a preceding statement or
			suggestion, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				870
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ra.</u>
				556
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1188
			</span></i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδενὸς μὲν οὖν ἄξιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Euthd.</u>
					305a
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγώ σοι οὐκ ἂν δυναίμην
				ἀντιλέγειν</span><i>;</i> Answ. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ
				μὲν οὖν τῇ ἀληθείᾳ δύνασαι ἀντιλέγειν</span> nay
			it is <i>not me, but rather</i> truth, that you cannot gainsay,
				<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				201c
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				18.140
			</span></i>:—so <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐμενοῦν .
				. γε,</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				1.20.1
			</span></i>; 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέν</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
				11.2
			</span></i>.</div>
